BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pinecone Animal Craft
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260720T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260720T150000
UID:6a24411b4407827f8aa3025a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Create your own adorable little forest animal using pinecones 
 and a variety of other fun materials.\nSo many amazing creatures in the na
 tural world depend on trees for food\, shelter\, nesting sites\, and habit
 at. Squirrels\, rabbits\, owls and foxes all depend on forests\, even here
  in the urban environment!\nTake Pinecones found locally in Long Branch an
 d your creativity to transform them into woodland creatures to take home w
 ith you. This fun\, hands-on craft is a great way to learn about trees whi
 le creating your very own forest-inspired crafts.\nInformation Collection 
 Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto
  Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, 
 and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registr
 ation\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles y
 our information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\
 n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Long Branch\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a24411b4407827f8aa3025a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
