SUMMARY:Scientists in School: Science Meets Art!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260707T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260707T150000
UID:69e7ffe8e7c57a539c143869@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Discover what happens when science meets art! Explore percepti
 on as you use shadows\, colour\, motion\, and light to create art from sci
 ence. You’ll make a puppet\, a spinning top and a kaleidoscope\, as well
  as design your own galaxy. “The greatest scientists are always artists 
 as well!” (Albert Einstein).\nFor school-aged children and their caregiv
 ers. Drop-in.\nUnfortunately\, we cannot accommodate any large groups/dayc
 ares for this program.
LOCATION:Jones\, Children's Area
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e7ffe8e7c57a539c143869
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Watermelon Fan Craft
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260828T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260828T150000
UID:6a285256c7d3cd58005f29f9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Summers can be hot wherever you are. A nice watermelon fan cra
 ft will keep your cool. Come to enjoy us to make your own adorable waterme
 lon fan. All materials will be provided. This program was designed for kid
 s 6-12. Younger kids are welcome with the help of their parents or caregiv
 ers.\nRegistration required.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe Personal
  Information on this form is collection by the Toronto Public Library unde
 r the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The infor
 mation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and
  evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can 
 be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 7
 89 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.​
LOCATION:Woodside Square\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a285256c7d3cd58005f29f9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:I Heart Drama Workshop Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T160000
UID:69cc3dfcad384e40edb8061e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Five-day workshop series\; learn drama skills\, play drama gam
 es\, try new ideas\, work together and make new friends. Registration inc
 ludes all five dates of this series (July 13\, 14\, 15\, 16 & 17).\nAges 7
 -10. Registration required.
LOCATION:Richview\, Lower Level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cc3dfcad384e40edb8061e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mausritter RPG
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260729T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260729T150000
UID:6a2c2ec816554cd59fc85d7f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:You are mere mice in an enormous world full of dangers: cats\
 , snakes\, and venomous spiders to name but a few! Fortunately you have we
 apons (of sorts): a fishhook fitted onto a twig\, a sewing needle or mayb
 e just a sharp stone lashed to a twig with some old tooth floss. You have
  allies as well\, and hopefully between you\, you also have a plan. Will t
 his be enough to defeat your enemies\, plunder their treasure and earn eve
 rlasting fame and glory? Much will depend on the plan\, and a little will
  depend on the dice!\nMausritter\nis a swords and whiskers role-playing ga
 me set in the vein of classic stories such as\nMouse Guard\nand\nRedwall\n
 . The stakes are high\,\,with perilous combat\, sneaky plans\, treasure an
 d a slim chance to become the heroes of your colony. Some mice may lose th
 eir lives (heroically of course)\, but you can just create a new mouse and
  play on!\nRegistration opens June 27th and is the best way to guarantee 
 a spot.\nAges 8-12 strongly recommended.\nInformation Collection Notice:\n
 The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public L
 ibrary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d)
 . The information will only be used for event and program registration\, d
 elivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your infor
 mation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-3
 97-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Rooms A & B/C
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2c2ec816554cd59fc85d7f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:K’NEX Construction Destruction
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260706T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260706T113000
UID:6a050690caf93436005bc944@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have fun and collaborate to imagine\, design\, and construct l
 ightweight\, high‑strength 3‑D bridges out of K’NEX. Test the streng
 th of your bridge using a specialized “Bridge‑Crusher” rig. Then lea
 rn how multiple designs and modifications can influence real‑world struc
 tural strength.\nSuitable for children ages 6 to 12.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a050690caf93436005bc944
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Blooms Acrylic Painting Workshop for Teens
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260706T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260706T153000
UID:6a038b48c6a1dc3d00d35101@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop Teens will create beautiful textured floral p
 aintings in acrylics. They will learn compositional techniques and a varie
 ty of acrylic painting techniques to create a background and colourful blo
 oms. They will be able to add depth to their paintings by adding highlight
 s\, shadows and details.\nThe program will take place in the Auditorium lo
 cated in the basement. Elevator on site. If you have any questions\, pleas
 e call Bendale Branch at 416-396-8910.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nTh
 e personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Lib
 rary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). 
 The information will only be used for event and program registration\, del
 ivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informa
 tion can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-59
 81\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Bendale\, Auditorium - Basement
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a038b48c6a1dc3d00d35101
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
