BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Advanced Robotics with Spike Prime
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T153000
UID:6a21d3f8c7d3cd58005e1dfa@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Hosted by ICE Robotics\, this engaging robotics and coding pr
 ogram will introduce participants to\nengineering\, programming\, and cre
 ative problem-solving using the LEGO® Education Spike Prime kit.\nDesign
 ed for children ages 9–12\n\, the program is suitable for both beginner
 s and those with previous robotics\nexperience.\nParticipants will design\
 , build\, and program their own robots while exploring STEM concepts thro
 ugh fun\, hands-on challenges. As they work through exciting projects\, p
 articipants will develop critical thinking\, teamwork\, creativity\, and 
 coding skills in an interactive and supportive learning environment.\nThi
 s program is for children ages 9-12 years old\n.\nInformation Collection N
 otice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto 
 Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, a
 nd 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registra
 tion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles yo
 ur information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n
 \, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Morningside\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a21d3f8c7d3cd58005e1dfa
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
