BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Scratch Coding Camp For Kids (Ages 8-12)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T160000
UID:6a29be7e1e67cd9cb338f1a1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn Scratch coding and create various games and projects!\nK
 ids will have the opportunity to learn the basics of block coding through 
 hands-on activities and engaging projects. They will explore how to create
  their own animations\, games\, and interactive stories using Scratch's si
 mple and intuitive interface.\nOur instructors will guide the participants
  through various coding concepts and help them unleash their creativity.\n
 No prior coding experience is required. This series is perfect for kids w
 ho are curious about coding and want to dive into the exciting world of te
 chnology.\nThis camp will take place from July 13th to July 16th. Partic
 ipants must attend all days of the camp.\nComputers will be provided for t
 his class.\nRegistration is required. Space is limited.\nInformation Colle
 ction Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the T
 oronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20
 (c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program r
 egistration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library han
 dles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@t
 pl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, 2nd floor Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a29be7e1e67cd9cb338f1a1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Movie and Paint: Flow
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T153000
UID:6a1e22d54dc267647dab69e9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:For ages 6 to 12.  Registration opens June 15.\nJoin us for a 
 special screening of\nFlow\n\, an animated film that follows a curious ca
 t exploring a surprising new world where water has taken over. As the cat 
 travels by boat through mysterious landscapes\, it meets other animals an
 d discovers moments of friendship\, danger\, and wonder. While you watch\,
  you’ll create your own watercolour painting inspired by the journey on 
 screen.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this 
 form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries
  Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be us
 ed for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions
  about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerl
 ine staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toro
 nto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Lower level program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1e22d54dc267647dab69e9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
