BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toys Alive! Exhibition Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T173000
UID:69fdddb5c6a1dc3d00d258a5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Curious about what your toys get up to when you are not lookin
 g? We jumped into the toy box to discover just that. From dolly’s advent
 ures to teddy bears on the search for honey to toy soldiers on patrol. Joi
 n us for a free guided tour of TD Gallery’s current exhibition Toys Aliv
 e! Explore literary works from the late 1800s to present day from the Osbo
 rne Collection of Early Children’s Books!\nRegistration is not required 
 but is encouraged. Please meet at the entrance to the TD Gallery.\nInforma
 tion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collecte
 d by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 
 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and
  program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the l
 ibrary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nan
 swerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, TD Gallery\, first floor of Toronto R
 eference Library
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fdddb5c6a1dc3d00d258a5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bill Russell: Du pays des bayous et des prairies
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260722T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260722T144500
UID:6a1f1b774407827f8aa21796@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:À partir de chants et histoires de la Louisiane\, Bill Russel
 l avive son jeune public. Tout le monde est invité à participer durant l
 e spectacle. Il raconte avec un sourire dans un coin de la bouche le pass
 é et le présent des Cajuns et leurs liens avec les Acadiens. Ages 6-12.
  Drop-in.\nAccessibilité:\nLe sous-titrage en direct ou automatique\, l
 ’interprétation en langue des signes\, les services d’intervenant\, o
 u les services d’accompagnement sont disponibles sur demande. Veuillez 
 soumettre votre demande au moins deux semaines à l’avance à : tpl.ca/a
 ccessibility-events
LOCATION:Richview\, Lower Level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1f1b774407827f8aa21796
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bead-a-Sea Adventure
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T150000
UID:6a1f31d9f56bd86e00b4020f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:For ages 6 to 12.  Registration opens June 15.\nDive into cre
 ativity with our "Undersea Adventure" Perler Bead program! Design vibrant 
 sea creatures like turtles\, dolphins\, and starfish\, using colorful bead
 s and pegboards. Once ironed by staff\, participants will take home their 
 own ocean masterpieces.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal info
 rmation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the 
 Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information
  will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalu
 ation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dir
 ected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yon
 ge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Lower level program room
