SUMMARY:The Mathemagic Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260722T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260722T163000
UID:6a0730c0c6a1dc3d00d3e9ad@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​'The Mathemagic Show' is based on mathematics\, numbers\, t
 he power of the brain\, the Rubik's cube\, magic\, and comedy. Performer M
 ikael Taieb's goal is to demonstrate how easy\, simple\, fun\, magic and a
 rtistic Mathematics can be!\nOfficial Rubik’s Cube Ambassador\, Creator 
 of the Live Stage Pixel Art\, the Two-Sided Pixel Art and the CO2 Pixel Ar
 t\, Mikael Taieb is a leading authority and one of the most revolutionary 
 Rubik’s cube performance artists. Utilizing his own personally crafted a
 nd one-of-a-kind techniques to create stunning art pieces like no other\, 
 incredibly fast-live on stage. He will amaze and perplex audiences with hi
 s unique blend of magic\, humour\, and visual artistry.\nInformation Colle
 ction Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the T
 oronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20
 (c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program r
 egistration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library han
 dles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@t
 pl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0730c0c6a1dc3d00d3e9ad
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
