BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wonder Workshop: Pollinators Challenge
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T150000
UID:6a075f5ac6a1dc3d00d3f458@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wondered at the beauty of a monarch butterfly an
 d what they overcome to survive? What would happen if these important poll
 inators disappeared? Join us to learn all about the journey of the monarch
  butterfly. Then use your imagination to design and build your own mock bu
 tterfly garden station. Plus\, enter a prize draw for a chance to win an a
 wesome book. For kids ages 6 to 12. Space is limited.\nInformation Collect
 ion Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Tor
 onto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c
 )\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program reg
 istration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handl
 es your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl
 .ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Woodside Square\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a075f5ac6a1dc3d00d3f458
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nadja Lubiw-Hazard: Tizzy and Me: Fifteen Ways to Love a Mink
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T113000
UID:6a060ada748daf857d58a442@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join author and veterinarian Nadja Lubiw-Hazard for an interac
 tive storytelling program as she reads from her children's chapter book\, 
 Tizzy and Me: Fifteen Ways to Love a Mink. The story is narrated by spunky
  seven-year-old Georgia\, who lives with her two moms and their dog\, Tizz
 y. This story celebrates animal activism and 2SLGBTQ+ families. Following 
 the reading\, there will be a Q&A with the author\, and a storytelling act
 ivity using story stones.\nNadja is a veterinarian turned writer. She writ
 es for both adults and children. As a life-long animal lover and long time
  advocate for them\, Nadja loves to share her passion for animals and natu
 re wherever she goes. She lives in Toronto with her wife\, and a fluffy fe
 isty white cat.\nNo registration required. For children aged 6-12.
LOCATION:Hillcrest\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a060ada748daf857d58a442
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
