BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Leaf Printing Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T190000
UID:6a243c1df56bd86e00b4ed1b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Use a variety of real local leaves to make beautiful painted a
 rt prints on a range of paper and fabric. During this workshop create gree
 ting cards\, bookmarks\, art prints\, fabric patches\, and other crafts to
  take home with you. Consider bringing a tote bag or other item that you w
 ould like to decorate through leaf printing.\nYou'll also be able to learn
  from urban Forest Researcher summer students from the Long Branch Neighbo
 urhood Association\, different tree species for each leaf and share tip fo
 r telling them apart.\nCome join us for a special time making some beautif
 ul art pieces.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information o
 n this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Li
 braries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will onl
 y be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Qu
 estions about how the library handles your information can be directed to 
 Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street
 \, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Long Branch\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a243c1df56bd86e00b4ed1b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wonder Workshop: Pollinators Challenge
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260717T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260717T153000
UID:6a0777c143b41b3d0066c844@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wondered at the beauty of a monarch butterfly an
 d what they overcome to survive? What would happen if these important poll
 inators disappeared? Join us to learn all about the journey of the monarch
  butterfly. Then use your imagination to design and build your own mock bu
 tterfly garden station. Plus\, enter a prize draw for a chance to win an a
 wesome book. For kids ages 6 to 10. Space is limited.
LOCATION:Annette Street\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0777c143b41b3d0066c844
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
