DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T160000
UID:6a2d6fce361280dd22643401@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:For ages 10 to 12.  Registration opens July 15.\nGet ready to
  laugh\, create\, and take the mic! In this fun and supportive 3-day mini 
 camp\, kids will learn the basics of stand-up comedy—how to write jokes\
 , build confidence\, and develop their own unique comedic voice. By the e
 nd of the program\, each participant will create a short 3-minute comedy s
 et to perform in a casual showcase for their friends and families. No exp
 erience needed—just a sense of humor and a willingness to try something 
 new!\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this for
 m is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Ac
 t\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used 
 for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions ab
 out how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline
